    "created_at": "2023-07-20T03:58:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-20T03:58:01Z",
    "body": "I don't have strong opinions either way, but I did want to say that despite this coming up in the context of a problem I was solving, I actually lean towards preserving this parse error.\r\n\r\nUnquoted URLs seem pretty fraught to me in general; even if your URL is composed entirely of [URL code points](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#url-code-points), `/` and `'` seem a bit dangerous too. (And `&` is definitely dangerous, although in a different way, and I believe it's conformant to have them unescaped in certain circumstances.)\r\n\r\nIn any case, thanks for filing to start the discussion!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
